# Newline policy: SQL migration bytes must check out as LF so anchored
# multiline matchers (dollar-quoted $old$ blocks compared against
# pg_get_functiondef output) see the same convention as stored definitions.
# This affects FUTURE checkouts only: it does not rewrite existing worktree
# files, restage anything, or repair already-installed function bodies.
# Existing CRLF worktree files keep their bytes until re-checked-out.
supabase/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
